@startuml

title The identity request: the steps to run, and what each one reports

class "identity workflow request\n(workflow.v1.start payload)" as req <<message>> #E1F5FF {
    {field} +steps : list of step requests
}

class "step request" as step <<message>> #E1F5FF {
    {field} +name : name
    {field} +behaviour : complete | warn | fail
    {field} +compensate : flag
    {field} +delay seconds : count
}

req "1" --> "*" step : declares, in order

note bottom of step
    behaviour defaults to complete, and a value
    the handler does not recognise fails the step
    rather than passing for a completion.
end note

note right of step
    compensate declares the step's compensation
    subject, which is what a later failure unwinds.
    delay holds the step before it reports, so a
    run can be observed in flight.
end note

@enduml
